# Generic fixtures

Names in code, tests, OpenSpec, commits, and docs are placeholders. They are not copied from this machine.

## Required

1. Device names, sink descriptions, camera models, hostnames, account names, thread ids, and similar values from local logs or hardware stay out of the repo.
2. Use generic placeholders such as «Headset Game», «Headset Chat», «Front Speakers», or «Webcam».
3. If a real local name landed in a new change, replace it before the commit.

## Do not

- Paste a name from a diagnostics log, stdout, or the hardware on this machine into a test, spec, or comment
